cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Build-and-Find, please cite the paper given under
  preferred-citation.
type: software
title: "Build-and-Find"
abstract: >-
  Build-and-Find is a protocol and benchmark for evaluating whether downstream
  coding agents can recover the intended behavior and design choices of a
  repository written by another agent, and how much inspection the recovery
  requires. This release contains the harness, two Rust task specifications
  with specification-traced multiple-choice question banks, the generated
  artifacts, run records, canonical tables, derived reports, Croissant
  metadata, and post-review audit records.
